        <body>
            <div xml:id="d273">

                <pb facs="0554" n="498" sameAs="frus:frus1876/pg498"/>

                <head>No. 263.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish
                        to Mr. Cushing.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-07-22"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 22,
                        1874</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 44.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Dispatches addressed by you to this
                    Department, numbered 38, 39, 40, 41, 42, 43, 44, 45, 46, and 47, have been
                    received.</p>
                <p>With reference to your No. 44, of the 27th ultimo, relating to the article
                    published by General Burriel in one of the newspapers of Madrid on the 14th of
                    April last, I have to state that your action, as therein set forth, is approved
                    by this Department.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
